WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:14.310
Unit 3 · Shapes, Grids & Coordinates · done!

3
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:20.070
Unit 4 · Thinking Like a Problem Solver

4
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.550
Chapter 1 · Estimation & Guess-Check-Improve

5
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:32.740
A coder's trick for tricky questions!

6
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:41.170
Riya finds a jar of laddoos at the mela

7
00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:46.630
"Guess how many laddoos and win the jar!"

8
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:51.520
The lid is sealed. No counting!

9
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:58.580
What should Riya do? Think!

10
00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:08.930
"A million!" "Three!" Do those make sense?

11
00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:17.790
Riya thinks: "Hmm, about 20?"

12
00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:22.580
That's called an ESTIMATE

13
00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:26.820
A sensible guess, close to the real answer

14
00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:40.140
Not exact · Not wild · Smart and close

15
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:46.460
Use what you know to guess well

16
00:01:46.460 --> 00:02:04.670
Pencil: about 15 cm, not 15 m, not 1 cm

17
00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:21.980
School bus: about 40 children

18
00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:32.100
Clues: too small · too big · just right

19
00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:39.590
Guess 20 → "Too small!" → go bigger

20
00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:49.220
Guess 30 → "Too big!" → between 20 and 30

21
00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:58.370
Guess 25 → "Just right!" Riya wins!

22
00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:10.140
Guess → Check → Improve

23
00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:17.270
Too small → go bigger. Too big → go smaller.

24
00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:34.340
40 is too big. 30 is too small. Where is it?

25
00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:39.790
Between 30 and 40!

26
00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:46.260
Secret number: between 1 and 100

27
00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:57.970
50 is too big · 25 is too small

28
00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:08.990
What's the smartest next guess?

29
00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:22.920
About 37 · halfway between 25 and 50

30
00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:29.040
Coders guess, check and improve too!

31
00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:41.820
Try → Test → Fix = debugging

32
00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:55.290
Meera's square: test, find the bug, fix it

33
00:04:55.290 --> 00:05:03.750
Riya's first guess was wrong. Is that bad?

34
00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:18.920
Every try teaches you something!

35
00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:26.290
How many steps across the hall?

36
00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:32.760
Hall ≈ 10 m · one step ≈ 50 cm

37
00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:44.020
2 steps = 1 m → 10 m ≈ 20 steps

38
00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:54.290
1,000 cm ÷ 50 cm = 20 steps

39
00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:59.670
Your turn: practice check

40
00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:13.410
1 m shelf · books 2 cm thick · how many?

41
00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:28.030
100 cm ÷ 2 cm = about 50 books

42
00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:33.910
Estimate = a sensible guess

43
00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:38.440
Guess → Check → Improve

44
00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:44.530
Too small → bigger · Too big → smaller

45
00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:50.080
First guesses can be wrong. Keep improving!

46
00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:56.480
Chapter 1 done!

47
00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:03.280
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
